{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03FA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$i : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nR^pi(\\mathcal{F}) = \\underline{H}^p(\\mathcal{F}) :\nU \\longmapsto H^p(U, \\mathcal{F})\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-locality}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-include-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:57f41bbcb64ab64570012ac59215efc0393ef6eae34063ff04c33ddb7afad612", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:10fbffb6845870b1b1b9a0620db1b46a099bf4bf898d0e0924c9881440e476ab", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nConsider the functor\n<MATH_0002>.\nIt is a left exact functor with right derived functors given by\n<MATH_0003>\nsee discussion in\nSection <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cc669921e5ec9c5602515ee4215d62e351d37bcbfe761f1aa9ad6e3ceca960e2", "unit_id": "tag:06YK:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03FA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0004": "$R^pi$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0007": "$R^pi(\\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\frac{\\Ker(\\mathcal{I}^n(U) \\to \\mathcal{I}^{n + 1}(U))}\n{\\Im(\\mathcal{I}^{n - 1}(U) \\to \\mathcal{I}^n(U))}.\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$H^p(U, \\mathcal{F})$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0e3d5bb2bda1c1cd212cd4d0d85fc599f5d8066a46a1b2f463c00b3fb66d704f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:13e5c57ade02cc382f630feb6dc73f3eec129c00618ee032516b0dce6fac74b9", "source_text": "It is clear that <MATH_0001> is left exact.\nChoose an injective resolution <MATH_0002>\nin <MATH_0003>.\nBy definition <MATH_0004> is the <MATH_0005>th cohomology <TEXTITOPEN_0001>presheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof the complex <MATH_0006>. In other words, the\nsections of <MATH_0007> over an object <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>\nare given by\n<MATH_0010>\nwhich is the definition of <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0a609ad38d09144ba2b87ceeed2b12c4cdf46c3ce22246624406809a62169f90", "unit_id": "tag:06YK:proof"}
